data.content:
The `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` 10.0 package upgraded from **OpenAPI.NET v1 to v2**, which has several breaking changes:

## Key Changes

| .NET 9 (OpenAPI.NET v1) | .NET 10 (OpenAPI.NET v2) |
|---|---|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` types (`OpenApiString`, etc.) | Removed — use native `JsonNode` |
| `param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString(...)` | `param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("...")` |
| `new OpenApiResponse { Description = ... }` | Same, but `Responses` is now `IDictionary<string, OpenApiResponse>` (not `OpenApiResponses`) |
| `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` inherits `Dictionary<...>` | Now has a `Schemes` property instead |
| `schema.Nullable = true/false` | Removed — use `schema.Type = JsonSchemaType.Null \| ...` (flags enum) |
| `schema.Required` is `ISet<string>` | Now on each property via `schema.Properties[key].Required` or similar |
| `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` | `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` (unchanged) |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // OpenAPI.NET v2: use JsonNode instead of OpenApiString
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };

    // v2: OpenApiSecurityRequirement no longer inherits Dictionary;
    // use the Schemes dictionary property instead
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new OpenApiSecurityRequirement
        {
            Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
            {
                [oAuthScheme] = scopes
            }
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            // v2: Nullable removed; instead manipulate the Type flags enum.
            // To mark as NOT nullable, ensure Null flag is absent:
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

## Summary of fixes

1. **Remove `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any`** — add `using System.Text.Json.Nodes`
2. **`OpenApiString` → `JsonValue.Create(...)`** for all example/default values
3. **`schema.Nullable`** — replaced by the `JsonSchemaType.Null` flag on `schema.Type`
4. **`OpenApiSecurityRequirement`** — no longer a dictionary itself; assign its `.Schemes` property
